<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title> 
<para>A ceramic sugar bowl weighs 340 grams when empty. It is then filled with sugar. One tablespoon of sugar weighs 12.5 grams.</para>

<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Write an equation to represent the relationship between the total weight of the
          bowl in grams, \( W \), and the tablespoons of sugar, \( T \).</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\( W=340 + 12.5T \), or \( 340 + 12.5T = 740 \)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>When the sugar bowl is full, it weighs 740 grams. How many tablespoons of sugar can the bowl hold? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>32 tablespoons;</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<exercise>
  <problem>
      <para>The graph represents the relationship between the number of tablespoons of sugar in the bowl and the total weight of the bowl.</para>

    <media><image alt="Graph of a line. Weight, grams. Sugar, tablespoons." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b1dadb12d00e370697db2a2a2d30229cbe3eab98"/>
    </media><para>Which point on the graph could represent your answer to the previous question?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Point D, because its coordinates could be (32, 740).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>About how many tablespoons of sugar are in the bowl when the total weight is 600 grams?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>About 21 tablespoons. Looking at the graph, when the weight is 600, the line is about at 21.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
</section>
</content>
